# madcide keybinding profile: neovim/vim — the MODAL personality
# (modes-as-scopes, owner ruling 2026-08-31). The unscoped lines are
# vim's CONTROL-key chords (the engine table — live in every mode);
# @normal / @insert are the vi mode tables the session's vi arm routes
# printable keys through. A profile carrying @normal data loads in
# NORMAL mode; ^N v (the modes palette) toggles modal editing off/on.
# Scoped keys match AS WRITTEN — spelling both cases is what makes the
# vi alphabet case-sensitive (a/A, i/I, o/O, x/X).
#
# The grammar (session machinery, not table data): counts multiply
# (3x, 2d3w = 6 words), d/c pend and double to the line-wise form
# (dd/cc), a count before G is a line number (5G), esc clears a
# pending count/operator. Honest absences, never pretended: no
# registers/put (y/p), no text objects (iw), no repeat (.), no gg
# (1G is the door), operator spans are byte-wise over the motion, and
# w/b are the shared end-of-word motions (dw is vim's `de` shape).
#
# vim's control chords
^r redo
^f pgdn
^b pgup
^d pgdn
^u pgup
^l refresh
# the ^W window family (vim's own seats on madcide's window verbs)
^w ^w nextw
^w s splitw
^w o onlywin
^w c killwin
^w + groww
^w - shrinkw
# madcide's IDE doors (control keys vim leaves unclaimed here; the rest
# of the IDE rides the colon line and the palettes)
^n modes
^p project
^t options
^k h help
^k ; check
^k i outline
^k a view
^k b build
^k e editfile
# vi NORMAL mode — motions
@normal h left
@normal j down
@normal k up
@normal l right
@normal w wordright
@normal b wordleft
@normal 0 home
@normal $ end
@normal G vigoto
# vi NORMAL mode — edits and commands
@normal x del
@normal X backspace
@normal u undo
@normal d videlete
@normal c vichange
@normal : colon
@normal / find
@normal n findnext
# vi NORMAL mode — insert entries
@normal i viinsert
@normal I viinsertbol
@normal a viappend
@normal A viappendeol
@normal o viopenbelow
@normal O viopenabove
# vi INSERT mode
@insert esc vinormal
